Z||000015||fierospeeder||05-23-2000||12:31 AM||||&lt;---going to stalk ironhorse,  just joking<P>Anyway, i have messed around on aol, for a long time, i wont say what.  <P>But it is impossible to blame anyone on aol, with text because anyone can create it and use anyones screennames which can be stolen from hackers, etc...  There is a better chance with email, but thats pretty much the same thing.  Tracking down someones IP is one way they can try to get you but its to much of a bother.  There are more serious crimes on the internet and on aol.  Mostly hacking into servers and stealing credit card info which is possible from a website.  I wouldn't worry about someone going to the EPA and basing it on the internet.  I seen people that have been harassed on the internet, and for them to complain about it, takes a lot of time and going through several courts just get something done.  Its not really taken seriously, except guys trying to get 15 year olds offline.<P>This guys probably an idiot, and drives a honda, and has nothing else better to do.||||reg||1
