Z||000018||Greg Piet||05-23-2000||03:58 AM||||I was really trying to avoid this whole thing, but I just couldnt resist.<P>I think the "im telling the EPA about you" thing is reminescent of NAZI's encouraging children to turn in their parents.  I would never NARC on a fellow Fierophile!<P>I saw a few posts talking loosely about engine thermodynamics, and the "physics" of combustion.  Are you people physicists?<P>I also saw a post about who are you going to believe, the old mechanic or the booksmart guy.  Some of us are both(or smack in the middle)!<P>And Finally:  One of my car DOES NOT have a cat converter, EGR thingys, and runs on LEADED gasoline so there!  And it was made in 1957!!!   Not only does it lack these things but according to a Smog sniffer in New Jersey it was cleaner than a 1984 chrysler LeBaron 2.2 litre 4 cylinder, with a feedback carb and more smog parts than I knew what to do with.  Oh yes the 1957 also gets better mileage!<P>I really hope this EPA thread thing dies soon, because I will not be able to contain myself for much longer about my views of the EPA in general.  Heck Oxygenated fuel can get me going for hours alone.<P>Thanks all for your time!<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 05-23-2000).]||||reg||1
