Z||000021||lennyb4||05-23-2000||08:35 AM||||Well as most of you already know i tend to keep my nose out of subjects like this..BUT..every man has his limits. I would like to set the record straight. 1st off my brother works for the EPA as a environmental specialist (no comments fellas  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ) Our cars are considered collectors cars and the only EPA requirements we have to meet are the mandatory E-checks. Other then that the EPA will NOT bother to investigate a persons car (this statement from the EPA thierselves). Now i have no cat, PCV, or air pump on my car. And if anyone wants to call the big bad EPA then i'll give you the f**king number. Why dont you just go back and crawl back under the rock you came from and leave us alone. Its pretty sad when a forum (whom i consider to be a big distant family) has to watch every word or statement in fear of someone ratting them out. Where i grew up (south side of the bronx) we have a statement.."Snitches get stitches"..<P>**Sorry for the long post fellas (and ladies) its just that having family in the EPA and listening to people threating with STUPID COMMENTS really burns me up. I mean come one were all adults (i think)..||||reg||6
Z||000022||1FST2M6||05-23-2000||10:55 AM||||OK I’m changing my handle to  1CLN-LECTRIC-2M6kv . I’ve pulled the motor out of my car and replaced it with a LP powered generator and 20 12volt batteries and a nice 4hp Dayton single phase 18turn-triple. I have evacuated the A/C system and sent it to a toxic waste facility, and paid my $20,000 in fines voluntarily so the Freon for my air can NEVER hurt our environment.<P><BR>GET A LIFE! I enjoy driving my car and enjoy driving on the twisty national forests roads even more. With the exception of NOx my car is at least 2 times cleaner than Georgia state recommends. Just cause you’ve taken your cat off or disconnected the egr doesn’t mean your causing all the worlds weather and O3 problems. What about all of us with fireplaces, charcoal grills,  gas lawnmowers, they don’t have Cats, or anything 2 stroke (with the exception of diesel) And I’m sure you probly think a diesel is polluting bad too… its ALL PARTICULATES!!! It’s biodegradable and less than 1/10th of 1% of it even remotely harmful gasses. Just because you can see it doesn’t mean it’s bad.. The Power plant about 25 miles away from me BELTS out something bad “cause I can see it” ITS WATER VAPOR! And according to my internal combustion Professor at Ga. Tech Dr. E. Sterling and his published textbook and the EPAs numbers less than 2% of all the worlds pollution is caused by automobiles!  2% is a lot but go after the nasty big companies instead looking the other way till the press finds out and denying your involvement. Happens at LEAST once a year you see it on the news… sorry for the rant but I have issues with someone whining about a few enthusiasts having a good time. <BR>||||reg||1
